tarried:
Spurs clicking hard and loud;
And where he tarried dropped his tear
On heads he left low-bowed.

tarrying:
From us she wandered now a year,
Her tarrying unknown;
If wilderness prevent her feet,

tardy:
And now I go.  Nor threat, nor easy vow
Of tardy kindness can avail thee now
With me, whence fear and faith alike are flown;

tare:
As over his ledger he bent his head;
I'm busy to-day with tare and tret,
And I have no time to fume and fret.

‘A happy life means prudent compromise;
The tare runs through the farmer’s garnered sheaves;
But though the gleaner’s apron holds pure wheat,

tarries:
And I would answer: Gone before;
It tarries veiled in paradise.
When once the morning star shall rise,

tardiest:
The sap will surely quicken soon or late,
The tardiest bird will twitter to a mate;
So Spring must dawn again with warmth and bloom,

tarantelle:
The days will rally, wreathing
Their crazy tarantelle;
And you must go on breathing,
